# NEW SERVERS (JOY SERVICES, handed over 2026-08-17) — GITIGNORED, do NOT commit.
# Covered by .gitignore:11 (`*.env`). This repo is PUBLIC — verify with
#   git check-ignore -v connections/new-servers.env
# before ever running `git add`. Never use `git add -f` on this file.
#
# Single quotes are deliberate: the Linux password contains `$` and `!`, which a
# shell would expand if unquoted. Read with:
#   set -a; . connections/new-servers.env; set +a
#
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# ⚠️  IP CORRECTION — the addresses first handed over were WRONG BY ONE DIGIT
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#   GIVEN:   138.250.101.222 / 138.250.101.52   → dead from 5 networks; whois
#            says 138.250.0.0/16 = Cranfield University, GB (JANET). Not JIVO.
#   ACTUAL:  138.252.101.222 / 138.252.101.52   → all ports open, 13 ms.
#            whois 138.252.101.0/24 = JOYSVC / JOY SERVICES, www.joy.services,
#            country IN. That is the vendor.
#
# Found by reading `last` on the OLD SAP box: the vendor's own root session on
# 2026-08-14 12:19 came FROM 138.252.101.52. If these ever go dark again, that
# login history is the fastest way to recover the real address.

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# ⚠️  ACCESS UPDATE 2026-08-17 ~22:50 — .222 IS IP-FILTERED (office-only)
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# From ~21:30 the box stopped answering home + VPS on ALL ports (ICMP too).
# It is NOT down: an OFFICE PC (Victus) reaches .222:22/30015/50000 fine (ping
# 14ms). So inbound is filtered to allow the office public IP, not home/VPS —
# regardless of the vendor saying "no whitelist/blacklist". (.52 on the same
# subnet is reachable from home, so the filter is per-HOST on .222, not subnet.)
#
# WORKING HOME PATH (same idea as the old jivo-sap-any tunnel):
#   run  ./connections/sap-office-bridge.sh   → opens local 13015→HANA, 15000→SL
#   through Victus (office PC parked on the VPS). VERIFIED: HANA 30,947 Oil
#   invoices + Service Layer login as manager, both through the bridge.
#   HANA env: connections/hana-office-bridge.env  |  SL: SAPB1_HOST=127.0.0.1 PORT=15000
#
# DURABLE FIX — ✅ DONE 2026-08-17 ~23:10 (option b, the true "old mechanism"):
#   On hanadb (.222): ~/vps-tunnel.sh + ~/vps-tunnel-guard.sh, kept alive by the
#   superadmin crontab (`* * * * *` guard + `@reboot`). The box dials OUT to the
#   VPS and parks:  VPS 127.0.0.1:47522->:22, :43015->:30015(HANA), :45000->:50000(SL).
#   VPS root authorized_keys has hanadb's restricted (port-forwarding-only) key;
#   hanadb's superadmin authorized_keys has this Mac's + the VPS's ed25519 keys.
#   24/7, no office PC needed. Survives reboots (@reboot) and drops (guard/min).
#
# HOW TO REACH IT (any machine, anytime):
#   shell:  ssh jivo-sap-new                         (~/.ssh/config alias, via VPS)
#   data:   ./connections/sap-home-bridge.sh         (localhost:13015 HANA, :15000 SL)
#           then hana-sql -env connections/hana-office-bridge.env  /  SAPB1_HOST=127.0.0.1 PORT=15000 sapb1
#   FleetPanel now watches this box (alias jivo-sap-new, was the dead jivo-sap-any).
#
# The office bridge (connections/sap-office-bridge.sh via Victus) is kept as an
# emergency fallback only — the VPS path above is the primary and is 24/7.
# The direct-.222 values below still work FOR OFFICE OPERATORS (they're whitelisted).
#
# --- New LINUX server — VERIFIED 2026-08-17 19:21 IST ---------------------
# Logged in OK as superadmin. hostname=hanadb, uptime 7d23h (up since ~2026-08-09).
# HANA is RUNNING here (4 hdb processes; 30013 + 30015 listening).
# Ports confirmed reachable from home ISP: 22, 30015, 50000.
NEWLNX_HOST='138.252.101.222'
NEWLNX_NAME='hanadb'
NEWLNX_USER='superadmin'
NEWLNX_PASS='Jivo!@#$2025'
NEWLNX_SSH_PORT='22'
NEWLNX_HANA_PORT='30015'
NEWLNX_SL_PORT='50000'

# --- New WINDOWS server — IDENTIFIED, attachments NOT yet verified --------
# CONFIRMED (2026-08-17 ~20:30): this IS ours. RDP TLS cert on 13579 = CN=Jivo-App1,
# issued 2026-08-06 — the successor to the old JIVO-APP file server.
# Reachable ports from home: 13579 (RDP), 80, 443 (a leftover web app throwing
# 500s, French test cert — NOT attachments, ignore). 3389 and 445 are CLOSED
# from outside — RDP is on 13579, same convention as the old box (103.89.45.25:13579).
#
# INTERNAL PATH TO THE FILES (this is the route, mirrors the old architecture):
#   internal subnet is 10.10.101.0/24 (public .222/.52 → internal 10.10.101.222/.52).
#   From the new Linux box `hanadb`, 10.10.101.52:445 IS OPEN and smbclient is
#   installed. That is how we'll read the ~105 GB of attachments — NOT from home
#   directly. (Note: 10.10.101.51 = a DIFFERENT tenant, RDP cert CN=M39-KNTEER,
#   NOT ours — do not touch it.)
#
# BLOCKER: the handed-over credential ADMIN.JIVO / Aqr@3609 is REJECTED for SMB
# (NT_STATUS_LOGON_FAILURE) in every format tried (bare, Jivo-App1\, JIVO\, ADMIN).
# It is almost certainly an RDP-only local login — on the OLD box, SMB used a
# SEPARATE 'ADMIN' account (see fleet-access.env JIVOAPP_SMB_*). Stopped after 5
# attempts to avoid a Windows account lockout on a production box.
# => NEED FROM VENDOR: the SMB/file-share username+password for Jivo-App1 (or open
#    445 to us), plus the share names. Old shares were Attachments_Oil/Mart/Bev +
#    OMS_Attachments; Attachments_Oil alone was 180,693 files / 65.2 GB.
NEWWIN_HOST='138.252.101.52'
NEWWIN_NAME='Jivo-App1'
NEWWIN_INTERNAL='10.10.101.52'
NEWWIN_RDP_PORT='13579'
NEWWIN_RDP_USER='ADMIN.JIVO'
NEWWIN_RDP_PASS='Aqr@3609'
NEWWIN_SMB_USER='ADMIN.JIVO'   # ✅ WORKS over SMB as of 2026-08-19 16:xx — vendor fixed the account
NEWWIN_SMB_PASS='Aqr@3609'   # ✅ VERIFIED over SMB 2026-08-22 from hanadb (same as RDP pass; field was blank before)''
# CREDENTIAL IS WRONG AS GIVEN — verified 2026-08-17 ~20:40 via RDP auth-only
# (xfreerdp +auth-only over the open 13579) AND smbclient. ADMIN.JIVO / Aqr@3609
# fails on BOTH with LOGON_FAILURE. Tested variants, all LOGON_FAILURE:
#   users: ADMIN.JIVO, Administrator, ADMIN, JIVO\ADMIN, Jivo-App1\ADMIN.JIVO
#   pw digit-transpositions of Aqr@3609: Aqr@3069, Aqr@3690, Aqr@6309, Aqr@3906
# No ACCOUNT_LOCKED after ~8 failed attempts → the box appears to have NO lockout
# policy (nothing was broken). Unlike the IP typo, there is no recoverable source
# of truth for this password on our side. => ASK VENDOR to RE-CONFIRM the exact
# Windows login (the IP they gave was already wrong by one digit, so a password
# transcription error is very plausible). RDP is on 138.252.101.52:13579.
NEWWIN_ROLE='attachments file server (replaces JIVO-APP / 20.20.45.25) — CONFIRMED Jivo-App1'

# --- HANA login on the new box -------------------------------------------
